window.MC_PROBLEMS = [{"id": 1, "slug": "lru-cache", "title": "LRU Cache", "difficulty": "Medium", "timeMin": 45, "summary": "Implement an LRU cache in Kotlin with O(1) get and put. Android machine coding interview question with hints, tests and a reference solution.", "description": "<h3>Problem</h3>\n<p>Design and implement a <strong>Least Recently Used (LRU) Cache</strong>. It should support <code>get</code> and <code>put</code> operations in <strong>O(1)</strong> time.</p>\n<div class=\"req-box\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Functional Requirements</div>\n<ul>\n<li><code>get(key)</code> — Return the value if the key exists, otherwise return <code>-1</code>. Accessing a key marks it as recently used.</li>\n<li><code>put(key, value)</code> — Insert or update the key-value pair. If the cache is at capacity, evict the least recently used entry before inserting.</li>\n</ul></div>\n<div class=\"req-box\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Non-Functional Requirements</div>\n<ul>\n<li>Both operations must run in O(1) time</li>\n<li>Capacity is fixed at construction time</li>\n</ul></div>\n<h3>Example</h3>\n<pre style=\"background:var(--bg2);padding:12px;border-radius:8px;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:1.7;overflow-x:auto\">val cache = LRUCache(2)\ncache.put(1, 1)\ncache.put(2, 2)\ncache.get(1)    // → 1  (1 is now most recent)\ncache.put(3, 3) // evicts key 2\ncache.get(2)    // → -1 (evicted)\ncache.get(3)    // → 3</pre>", "hints": ["What data structure gives you O(1) lookup by key?", "To track recency, you need to know both the most recent and least recent entries quickly. A doubly linked list lets you remove and add nodes in O(1) — combine it with a HashMap.", "Use a HashMap&lt;Int, Node&gt; where each Node is in a doubly linked list. On every get/put, move that node to the head (most recent). The tail is always the LRU candidate to evict."], "approach": "<h3>Data Structure</h3>\n<p>Use a <strong>HashMap + Doubly Linked List</strong>. The map gives O(1) access to any node. The linked list maintains recency order — head is most recent, tail is least recent.</p>\n<h3>Key Operations</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>get</strong>: Look up node in map → move to head → return value</li>\n<li><strong>put</strong>: If key exists, update + move to head. If new, add at head. If over capacity, remove tail node and its map entry.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"miss-box\"><div class=\"miss-box-title\">What most candidates miss</div>\n<ul>\n<li>Using <code>LinkedHashMap</code> shortcut — fine for production but expect a \"implement from scratch\" follow-up</li>\n<li>Forgetting to update the map when evicting the tail node</li>\n<li>Off-by-one: checking capacity <em>before</em> insertion vs <em>after</em></li>\n</ul></div>", "androidStudio": false, "editorCode": "//sampleStart\nclass LRUCache(private val capacity: Int) {\n    // TODO: Implement LRU Cache with O(1) get and put\n    // Hint: Think HashMap + Doubly Linked List\n\n    fun get(key: Int): Int {\n        // Return value for key, or -1 if not found\n        // Accessing a key marks it as most recently used\n        return -1\n    }\n\n    fun put(key: Int, value: Int) {\n        // Insert or update key-value pair\n        // If at capacity, evict the least recently used entry first\n    }\n}\n//sampleEnd\n\n// ---- Droidly test runner (hidden in the editor) ----\nprivate var passedCount = 0\nprivate var totalCount = 0\nprivate fun record(name: String, error: Throwable?) {\n    totalCount++\n    when (error) {\n        null -> { passedCount++; println(\"✓ $name\") }\n        is NotImplementedError -> println(\"✗ $name — not implemented yet\")\n        is AssertionError -> println(\"✗ $name — ${error.message}\")\n        else -> println(\"✗ $name — threw ${error::class.simpleName}: ${error.message}\")\n    }\n}\nfun test(name: String, body: () -> Unit) = record(name, runCatching(body).exceptionOrNull())\nfun <T> expect(actual: T, expected: T, what: String = \"\") {\n    if (actual != expected) throw AssertionError((if (what.isEmpty()) \"\" else \"$what: \") + \"expected $expected, got $actual\")\n}\nfun expectTrue(cond: Boolean, message: String) { if (!cond) throw AssertionError(message) }\nfun summary() {\n    println()\n    if (passedCount == totalCount) println(\"ALL \" + totalCount + \" TESTS PASSED\")\n    else println(\"\" + passedCount + \" of \" + totalCount + \" tests passed\")\n}\n\nfun main() {\n    test(\"get returns -1 for a missing key\") { expect(LRUCache(2).get(42), -1) }\n    test(\"put then get returns the value\") { val c = LRUCache(2); c.put(1, 10); expect(c.get(1), 10) }\n    test(\"evicts the least recently used key when full\") {\n        val c = LRUCache(2); c.put(1, 1); c.put(2, 2); c.put(3, 3)\n        expect(c.get(1), -1, \"key 1\"); expect(c.get(2), 2, \"key 2\"); expect(c.get(3), 3, \"key 3\")\n    }\n    test(\"get marks a key as recently used\") {\n        val c = LRUCache(2); c.put(1, 1); c.put(2, 2); c.get(1); c.put(3, 3)\n        expect(c.get(2), -1, \"key 2 should be evicted\"); expect(c.get(1), 1, \"key 1 should stay\")\n    }\n    test(\"put on an existing key updates it without evicting\") {\n        val c = LRUCache(2); c.put(1, 1); c.put(2, 2); c.put(1, 100)\n        expect(c.get(1), 100, \"key 1\"); expect(c.get(2), 2, \"key 2\")\n    }\n    test(\"updating a key also makes it most recent\") {\n        val c = LRUCache(2); c.put(1, 1); c.put(2, 2); c.put(1, 5); c.put(3, 3)\n        expect(c.get(2), -1, \"key 2 should be evicted\"); expect(c.get(1), 5, \"key 1\")\n    }\n    test(\"capacity 1 keeps only the latest key\") {\n        val c = LRUCache(1); c.put(1, 1); c.put(2, 2); expect(c.get(1), -1, \"key 1\"); expect(c.get(2), 2, \"key 2\")\n    }\n    test(\"handles 100,000 operations quickly (O(1))\") {\n        val c = LRUCache(1000); val start = System.nanoTime()\n        for (i in 0 until 100_000) { c.put(i, i); c.get(i - 500) }\n        expect(c.get(99_999), 99_999); expect(c.get(98_000), -1, \"old key\")\n        expectTrue((System.nanoTime() - start) / 1_000_000 < 2000, \"took too long — is get/put O(n)?\")\n    }\n    summary()\n}\n", "solution": "class LRUCache(private val capacity: Int) {\n    private class Node(val key: Int, var value: Int) {\n        var prev: Node? = null\n        var next: Node? = null\n    }\n\n    private val map = HashMap<Int, Node>()\n    private val head = Node(0, 0)   // sentinel: most recent side\n    private val tail = Node(0, 0)   // sentinel: least recent side\n\n    init { head.next = tail; tail.prev = head }\n\n    fun get(key: Int): Int {\n        val node = map[key] ?: return -1\n        moveToFront(node)\n        return node.value\n    }\n\n    fun put(key: Int, value: Int) {\n        val existing = map[key]\n        if (existing != null) {\n            existing.value = value\n            moveToFront(existing)\n            return\n        }\n        if (map.size == capacity) {\n            val lru = tail.prev!!\n            unlink(lru)\n            map.remove(lru.key)\n        }\n        val node = Node(key, value)\n        map[key] = node\n        addFront(node)\n    }\n\n    private fun unlink(n: Node) { n.prev!!.next = n.next; n.next!!.prev = n.prev }\n    private fun addFront(n: Node) { n.next = head.next; n.prev = head; head.next!!.prev = n; head.next = n }\n    private fun moveToFront(n: Node) { unlink(n); addFront(n) }\n}\n", "tests": ["get returns -1 for a missing key", "put then get returns the value", "evicts the least recently used key when full", "get marks a key as recently used", "put on an existing key updates it without evicting", "updating a key also makes it most recent", "capacity 1 keeps only the latest key", "handles 100,000 operations quickly (O(1))"]}, {"id": 2, "slug": "token-bucket-rate-limiter", "title": "Token Bucket Rate Limiter", "difficulty": "Medium", "timeMin": 40, "summary": "Build a per-user token bucket rate limiter in Kotlin with lazy refill. Android machine coding question with hints, tests and a solution.", "description": "<h3>Problem</h3>\n<p>Implement a <strong>Token Bucket Rate Limiter</strong> that controls how many requests each user can make per second.</p>\n<div class=\"req-box\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Functional Requirements</div>\n<ul>\n<li><code>isAllowed(userId)</code> — Return <code>true</code> if the request is permitted, <code>false</code> if rate limited</li>\n<li>Each user gets their own independent bucket</li>\n<li>Bucket refills at a fixed rate over time (not just at fixed intervals)</li>\n<li>Bucket has a max capacity — tokens don't accumulate beyond it</li>\n</ul></div>\n<div class=\"req-box\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Token Bucket Rules</div>\n<ul>\n<li>Each request consumes 1 token</li>\n<li>Tokens refill continuously at <code>refillRatePerSecond</code></li>\n<li>If bucket is empty → request is denied</li>\n<li>Users start with a full bucket</li>\n</ul></div>", "hints": ["You don't need an actual background thread to refill tokens. How can you calculate how many tokens should have been added since the last request, using only the current timestamp?", "Store the last-access timestamp per user. On each request, compute elapsed time → multiply by refill rate → add tokens (capped at maxTokens).", "Use a data class to hold each user's current token count and last refill timestamp. Use System.currentTimeMillis() for time tracking."], "approach": "<h3>Lazy Refill Strategy</h3>\n<p>Don't use a background thread. Instead, calculate tokens lazily: on each request, check how much time has elapsed since the last request for that user, compute how many tokens should have been added, and top up the bucket.</p>\n<h3>Per-user State</h3>\n<pre style=\"background:var(--bg2);padding:10px;border-radius:8px;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px\">data class Bucket(\n  var tokens: Double,\n  var lastRefillTime: Long\n)</pre>\n<div class=\"miss-box\"><div class=\"miss-box-title\">What most candidates miss</div>\n<ul>\n<li>Using integer tokens instead of Double — causes precision loss with fractional refill rates</li>\n<li>Not capping tokens at <code>maxTokens</code> after refill</li>\n<li>Thread safety — a real implementation needs synchronization per user bucket</li>\n</ul></div>", "androidStudio": false, "editorCode": "//sampleStart\nclass TokenBucketRateLimiter(\n    private val maxTokens: Int,\n    private val refillRatePerSecond: Double\n) {\n    // TODO: Implement token bucket rate limiter\n    // Each userId gets its own bucket\n    // Tokens refill continuously over time (use lazy refill on each call)\n\n    fun isAllowed(userId: String): Boolean {\n        // Return true if request should be allowed, false if rate limited\n        return false\n    }\n}\n//sampleEnd\n\n// ---- Droidly test runner (hidden in the editor) ----\nprivate var passedCount = 0\nprivate var totalCount = 0\nprivate fun record(name: String, error: Throwable?) {\n    totalCount++\n    when (error) {\n        null -> { passedCount++; println(\"✓ $name\") }\n        is NotImplementedError -> println(\"✗ $name — not implemented yet\")\n        is AssertionError -> println(\"✗ $name — ${error.message}\")\n        else -> println(\"✗ $name — threw ${error::class.simpleName}: ${error.message}\")\n    }\n}\nfun test(name: String, body: () -> Unit) = record(name, runCatching(body).exceptionOrNull())\nfun <T> expect(actual: T, expected: T, what: String = \"\") {\n    if (actual != expected) throw AssertionError((if (what.isEmpty()) \"\" else \"$what: \") + \"expected $expected, got $actual\")\n}\nfun expectTrue(cond: Boolean, message: String) { if (!cond) throw AssertionError(message) }\nfun summary() {\n    println()\n    if (passedCount == totalCount) println(\"ALL \" + totalCount + \" TESTS PASSED\")\n    else println(\"\" + passedCount + \" of \" + totalCount + \" tests passed\")\n}\n\nfun main() {\n    test(\"a new user starts with a full bucket (3 requests pass)\") {\n        val l = TokenBucketRateLimiter(3, 1.0); repeat(3) { expect(l.isAllowed(\"u1\"), true, \"request ${it + 1}\") }\n    }\n    test(\"the request after the burst is denied\") {\n        val l = TokenBucketRateLimiter(3, 1.0); repeat(3) { l.isAllowed(\"u1\") }; expect(l.isAllowed(\"u1\"), false)\n    }\n    test(\"each user has an independent bucket\") {\n        val l = TokenBucketRateLimiter(2, 1.0); repeat(3) { l.isAllowed(\"u1\") }; expect(l.isAllowed(\"u2\"), true, \"u2\")\n    }\n    test(\"tokens refill over time\") {\n        val l = TokenBucketRateLimiter(1, 10.0); expect(l.isAllowed(\"u1\"), true, \"first\"); expect(l.isAllowed(\"u1\"), false, \"second\")\n        Thread.sleep(150); expect(l.isAllowed(\"u1\"), true, \"after 150ms at 10 tokens/s\")\n    }\n    test(\"refill never goes above maxTokens\") {\n        val l = TokenBucketRateLimiter(3, 20.0); repeat(3) { l.isAllowed(\"u1\") }\n        Thread.sleep(400)   // would be 8 tokens without the cap\n        var allowed = 0; repeat(6) { if (l.isAllowed(\"u1\")) allowed++ }\n        expect(allowed, 3, \"requests allowed after a long wait\")\n    }\n    test(\"fractional refill works (no integer rounding)\") {\n        val l = TokenBucketRateLimiter(1, 4.0); l.isAllowed(\"u1\")\n        Thread.sleep(150); expect(l.isAllowed(\"u1\"), false, \"0.6 tokens is not enough\")\n        Thread.sleep(150); expect(l.isAllowed(\"u1\"), true, \"1.2 tokens is enough\")\n    }\n    summary()\n}\n", "solution": "class TokenBucketRateLimiter(\n    private val maxTokens: Int,\n    private val refillRatePerSecond: Double\n) {\n    private class Bucket(var tokens: Double, var lastRefillNanos: Long)\n\n    private val buckets = HashMap<String, Bucket>()\n\n    @Synchronized\n    fun isAllowed(userId: String): Boolean {\n        val now = System.nanoTime()\n        val bucket = buckets.getOrPut(userId) { Bucket(maxTokens.toDouble(), now) }\n        val elapsedSeconds = (now - bucket.lastRefillNanos) / 1_000_000_000.0\n        bucket.tokens = minOf(maxTokens.toDouble(), bucket.tokens + elapsedSeconds * refillRatePerSecond)\n        bucket.lastRefillNanos = now\n        if (bucket.tokens >= 1.0) {\n            bucket.tokens -= 1.0\n            return true\n        }\n        return false\n    }\n}\n", "tests": ["a new user starts with a full bucket (3 requests pass)", "the request after the burst is denied", "each user has an independent bucket", "tokens refill over time", "refill never goes above maxTokens", "fractional refill works (no integer rounding)"]}, {"id": 3, "slug": "event-bus", "title": "Event Bus", "difficulty": "Medium", "timeMin": 35, "summary": "Implement a publish-subscribe event bus in Kotlin: subscribe, unsubscribe, publish. Android machine coding question with tests and a solution.", "description": "<h3>Problem</h3>\n<p>Implement a <strong>publish-subscribe Event Bus</strong> that allows components to communicate without direct references to each other.</p>\n<div class=\"req-box\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Functional Requirements</div>\n<ul>\n<li><code>subscribe(eventType, listener)</code> — Register a listener for an event type. Returns a unique <code>subscriptionId</code>.</li>\n<li><code>unsubscribe(subscriptionId)</code> — Remove a specific subscription</li>\n<li><code>publish(eventType, data)</code> — Notify all active listeners for that event type</li>\n<li>Multiple listeners can subscribe to the same event type</li>\n<li>Unsubscribing one listener should not affect others</li>\n</ul></div>", "hints": ["What data structure lets you look up all listeners for a given event type instantly?", "Use a Map&lt;String, Map&lt;String, Listener&gt;&gt; — outer key is eventType, inner key is subscriptionId. This gives O(1) subscribe, unsubscribe, and publish.", "For subscriptionId, use a UUID or a simple incrementing counter. Store a reverse mapping (subscriptionId → eventType) so unsubscribe doesn't need to scan all event types."], "approach": "<h3>Data Structure</h3>\n<p>Use two maps: <code>listeners: Map&lt;EventType, Map&lt;SubId, Listener&gt;&gt;</code> and <code>subscriptionIndex: Map&lt;SubId, EventType&gt;</code>. The second map makes unsubscribe O(1) without scanning.</p>\n<div class=\"miss-box\"><div class=\"miss-box-title\">What most candidates miss</div>\n<ul>\n<li>ConcurrentModificationException — if a listener modifies subscriptions during publish, iterate a copy</li>\n<li>Memory leaks — not cleaning up empty event type entries after all listeners unsubscribe</li>\n<li>Not handling the case where <code>unsubscribe</code> is called with an invalid ID</li>\n</ul></div>", "androidStudio": false, "editorCode": "//sampleStart\nclass EventBus {\n    // TODO: Implement a publish-subscribe event bus\n    // subscribe returns a unique subscriptionId that can be used to unsubscribe\n\n    fun subscribe(eventType: String, listener: (Any) -> Unit): String {\n        TODO(\"Implement subscribe — return a unique subscriptionId\")\n    }\n\n    fun unsubscribe(subscriptionId: String) {\n        TODO(\"Implement unsubscribe\")\n    }\n\n    fun publish(eventType: String, data: Any) {\n        TODO(\"Implement publish — notify all active listeners\")\n    }\n}\n//sampleEnd\n\n// ---- Droidly test runner (hidden in the editor) ----\nprivate var passedCount = 0\nprivate var totalCount = 0\nprivate fun record(name: String, error: Throwable?) {\n    totalCount++\n    when (error) {\n        null -> { passedCount++; println(\"✓ $name\") }\n        is NotImplementedError -> println(\"✗ $name — not implemented yet\")\n        is AssertionError -> println(\"✗ $name — ${error.message}\")\n        else -> println(\"✗ $name — threw ${error::class.simpleName}: ${error.message}\")\n    }\n}\nfun test(name: String, body: () -> Unit) = record(name, runCatching(body).exceptionOrNull())\nfun <T> expect(actual: T, expected: T, what: String = \"\") {\n    if (actual != expected) throw AssertionError((if (what.isEmpty()) \"\" else \"$what: \") + \"expected $expected, got $actual\")\n}\nfun expectTrue(cond: Boolean, message: String) { if (!cond) throw AssertionError(message) }\nfun summary() {\n    println()\n    if (passedCount == totalCount) println(\"ALL \" + totalCount + \" TESTS PASSED\")\n    else println(\"\" + passedCount + \" of \" + totalCount + \" tests passed\")\n}\n\nfun main() {\n    test(\"subscribe returns unique ids\") {\n        val b = EventBus(); val a = b.subscribe(\"A\") {}; val c = b.subscribe(\"A\") {}; expectTrue(a != c, \"ids must differ\")\n    }\n    test(\"publish notifies every listener of that type\") {\n        val b = EventBus(); val got = mutableListOf<String>()\n        b.subscribe(\"ORDER\") { got += \"L1:$it\" }; b.subscribe(\"ORDER\") { got += \"L2:$it\" }\n        b.publish(\"ORDER\", \"#1\"); expect(got.sorted(), listOf(\"L1:#1\", \"L2:#1\"))\n    }\n    test(\"listeners of other event types are not called\") {\n        val b = EventBus(); var calls = 0; b.subscribe(\"PAYMENT\") { calls++ }; b.publish(\"ORDER\", \"x\"); expect(calls, 0)\n    }\n    test(\"unsubscribe stops only that listener\") {\n        val b = EventBus(); val got = mutableListOf<String>()\n        val id1 = b.subscribe(\"ORDER\") { got += \"L1\" }; b.subscribe(\"ORDER\") { got += \"L2\" }\n        b.unsubscribe(id1); b.publish(\"ORDER\", \"x\"); expect(got, listOf(\"L2\"))\n    }\n    test(\"publishing with no listeners does not crash\") { EventBus().publish(\"NOBODY\", 1) }\n    test(\"unsubscribing an unknown id does not crash\") { EventBus().unsubscribe(\"does-not-exist\") }\n    test(\"a listener can unsubscribe itself while being notified\") {\n        val b = EventBus(); var calls = 0; lateinit var id: String\n        id = b.subscribe(\"E\") { calls++; b.unsubscribe(id) }; b.subscribe(\"E\") { calls++ }\n        b.publish(\"E\", 1); b.publish(\"E\", 2); expect(calls, 3, \"total calls\")\n    }\n    summary()\n}\n", "solution": "class EventBus {\n    private val listeners = HashMap<String, LinkedHashMap<String, (Any) -> Unit>>()\n    private val typeOf = HashMap<String, String>()   // subscriptionId -> eventType\n    private var nextId = 0\n\n    @Synchronized\n    fun subscribe(eventType: String, listener: (Any) -> Unit): String {\n        val id = \"sub-${++nextId}\"\n        listeners.getOrPut(eventType) { LinkedHashMap() }[id] = listener\n        typeOf[id] = eventType\n        return id\n    }\n\n    @Synchronized\n    fun unsubscribe(subscriptionId: String) {\n        val type = typeOf.remove(subscriptionId) ?: return   // unknown id: nothing to do\n        val forType = listeners[type] ?: return\n        forType.remove(subscriptionId)\n        if (forType.isEmpty()) listeners.remove(type)         // no empty entries left behind\n    }\n\n    fun publish(eventType: String, data: Any) {\n        val snapshot = synchronized(this) { listeners[eventType]?.values?.toList() } ?: return\n        snapshot.forEach { it(data) }                        // a copy, so listeners may (un)subscribe safely\n    }\n}\n", "tests": ["subscribe returns unique ids", "publish notifies every listener of that type", "listeners of other event types are not called", "unsubscribe stops only that listener", "publishing with no listeners does not crash", "unsubscribing an unknown id does not crash", "a listener can unsubscribe itself while being notified"]}, {"id": 4, "slug": "pagination-manager", "title": "Pagination Manager", "difficulty": "Easy", "timeMin": 25, "summary": "Write a pagination manager in Kotlin: pages, navigation and bounds checks. Android machine coding question with hints, tests and a solution.", "description": "<h3>Problem</h3>\n<p>Implement a <strong>Pagination Manager</strong> that splits a dataset into pages and supports navigation.</p>\n<div class=\"req-box\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Functional Requirements</div>\n<ul>\n<li><code>getPage(pageNumber)</code> — Return the correct slice of items for that page (1-indexed)</li>\n<li><code>nextPage(current)</code> — Return the next page or <code>null</code> if on last page</li>\n<li><code>previousPage(current)</code> — Return the previous page or <code>null</code> if on first page</li>\n<li>Each <code>Page</code> object carries: items, currentPage, totalPages, hasNext, hasPrevious</li>\n<li>Page numbers outside <code>1..totalPages</code> throw <code>IllegalArgumentException</code></li>\n</ul></div>\n<h3>Example</h3>\n<pre style=\"background:var(--bg2);padding:12px;border-radius:8px;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px\">// 23 items, pageSize = 5 → 5 pages\n// Page 1: [1,2,3,4,5]\n// Page 5: [21,22,23]  ← last page may be smaller</pre>", "hints": ["Total pages = ceil(totalItems / pageSize). Use integer math: (totalItems + pageSize - 1) / pageSize", "For page N, the start index is (N-1) * pageSize. The end index is min(startIndex + pageSize, totalItems).", "Validate pageNumber bounds — throw or return an empty page for out-of-range requests."], "approach": "<h3>Index Calculation</h3>\n<p>Page N (1-indexed): <code>startIndex = (pageNumber - 1) * pageSize</code>, <code>endIndex = min(startIndex + pageSize, items.size)</code>. Total pages: <code>ceil(items.size / pageSize.toFloat()).toInt()</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"miss-box\"><div class=\"miss-box-title\">What most candidates miss</div>\n<ul>\n<li>Off-by-one on the last page when items don't divide evenly</li>\n<li>Not validating out-of-bounds page numbers</li>\n<li>Using 0-indexed pages when the spec says 1-indexed</li>\n</ul></div>", "androidStudio": false, "editorCode": "import kotlin.math.ceil\n\n//sampleStart\ndata class Page<T>(\n    val items: List<T>,\n    val currentPage: Int,\n    val totalPages: Int,\n    val hasNext: Boolean,\n    val hasPrevious: Boolean\n)\n\nclass PaginationManager<T>(\n    private val allItems: List<T>,\n    private val pageSize: Int\n) {\n    fun getPage(pageNumber: Int): Page<T> {\n        TODO(\"Return the correct page — validate bounds, compute slice\")\n    }\n\n    fun nextPage(currentPage: Int): Page<T>? {\n        TODO(\"Return next page or null if already on last page\")\n    }\n\n    fun previousPage(currentPage: Int): Page<T>? {\n        TODO(\"Return previous page or null if already on first page\")\n    }\n}\n//sampleEnd\n\n// ---- Droidly test runner (hidden in the editor) ----\nprivate var passedCount = 0\nprivate var totalCount = 0\nprivate fun record(name: String, error: Throwable?) {\n    totalCount++\n    when (error) {\n        null -> { passedCount++; println(\"✓ $name\") }\n        is NotImplementedError -> println(\"✗ $name — not implemented yet\")\n        is AssertionError -> println(\"✗ $name — ${error.message}\")\n        else -> println(\"✗ $name — threw ${error::class.simpleName}: ${error.message}\")\n    }\n}\nfun test(name: String, body: () -> Unit) = record(name, runCatching(body).exceptionOrNull())\nfun <T> expect(actual: T, expected: T, what: String = \"\") {\n    if (actual != expected) throw AssertionError((if (what.isEmpty()) \"\" else \"$what: \") + \"expected $expected, got $actual\")\n}\nfun expectTrue(cond: Boolean, message: String) { if (!cond) throw AssertionError(message) }\nfun summary() {\n    println()\n    if (passedCount == totalCount) println(\"ALL \" + totalCount + \" TESTS PASSED\")\n    else println(\"\" + passedCount + \" of \" + totalCount + \" tests passed\")\n}\n\nfun main() {\n    val m = PaginationManager((1..23).toList(), pageSize = 5)\n    test(\"page 1 has the first 5 items\") { expect(m.getPage(1).items, listOf(1, 2, 3, 4, 5)) }\n    test(\"total pages rounds up (23 items / 5 = 5 pages)\") { expect(m.getPage(1).totalPages, 5) }\n    test(\"last page holds the remainder\") { expect(m.getPage(5).items, listOf(21, 22, 23)) }\n    test(\"hasNext / hasPrevious on first, middle and last page\") {\n        expect(m.getPage(1).hasPrevious, false, \"p1 hasPrevious\"); expect(m.getPage(1).hasNext, true, \"p1 hasNext\")\n        expect(m.getPage(3).hasPrevious, true, \"p3 hasPrevious\"); expect(m.getPage(3).hasNext, true, \"p3 hasNext\")\n        expect(m.getPage(5).hasNext, false, \"p5 hasNext\")\n    }\n    test(\"nextPage and previousPage navigate\") {\n        expect(m.nextPage(1)?.currentPage, 2, \"next of 1\"); expect(m.previousPage(3)?.currentPage, 2, \"previous of 3\")\n    }\n    test(\"nextPage on the last page and previousPage on the first return null\") {\n        expect(m.nextPage(5), null, \"next of 5\"); expect(m.previousPage(1), null, \"previous of 1\")\n    }\n    test(\"exact division has no empty last page\") {\n        val e = PaginationManager((1..10).toList(), 5); expect(e.getPage(1).totalPages, 2); expect(e.getPage(2).items, listOf(6, 7, 8, 9, 10))\n    }\n    test(\"out-of-range page numbers throw IllegalArgumentException\") {\n        for (n in listOf(0, -1, 6)) {\n            val err = runCatching { m.getPage(n) }.exceptionOrNull()\n            expectTrue(err is IllegalArgumentException, \"getPage($n) should throw IllegalArgumentException, got ${err?.let { it::class.simpleName } ?: \"no exception\"}\")\n        }\n    }\n    summary()\n}\n", "solution": "data class Page<T>(\n    val items: List<T>,\n    val currentPage: Int,\n    val totalPages: Int,\n    val hasNext: Boolean,\n    val hasPrevious: Boolean\n)\n\nclass PaginationManager<T>(\n    private val allItems: List<T>,\n    private val pageSize: Int\n) {\n    init { require(pageSize > 0) { \"pageSize must be positive\" } }\n\n    private val totalPages = ceil(allItems.size / pageSize.toDouble()).toInt()\n\n    fun getPage(pageNumber: Int): Page<T> {\n        require(pageNumber in 1..totalPages) { \"Page $pageNumber is out of range 1..$totalPages\" }\n        val start = (pageNumber - 1) * pageSize\n        val end = minOf(start + pageSize, allItems.size)\n        return Page(\n            items = allItems.subList(start, end),\n            currentPage = pageNumber,\n            totalPages = totalPages,\n            hasNext = pageNumber < totalPages,\n            hasPrevious = pageNumber > 1\n        )\n    }\n\n    fun nextPage(currentPage: Int): Page<T>? = if (currentPage < totalPages) getPage(currentPage + 1) else null\n\n    fun previousPage(currentPage: Int): Page<T>? = if (currentPage > 1) getPage(currentPage - 1) else null\n}\n", "tests": ["page 1 has the first 5 items", "total pages rounds up (23 items / 5 = 5 pages)", "last page holds the remainder", "hasNext / hasPrevious on first, middle and last page", "nextPage and previousPage navigate", "nextPage on the last page and previousPage on the first return null", "exact division has no empty last page", "out-of-range page numbers throw IllegalArgumentException"]}, {"id": 5, "slug": "retry-with-exponential-backoff", "title": "Retry with Exponential Backoff", "difficulty": "Medium", "timeMin": 40, "summary": "Retry a suspending call with exponential backoff using Kotlin coroutines. Android machine coding question with tests and a reference solution.", "description": "<h3>Problem</h3>\n<p>Implement a <strong>retry mechanism with exponential backoff</strong> that wraps any suspending function and retries it automatically on failure.</p>\n<div class=\"req-box\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Functional Requirements</div>\n<ul>\n<li>Retry up to <code>maxAttempts</code> times on exception</li>\n<li>Delay between retries grows exponentially: <code>initialDelay × multiplier^attempt</code></li>\n<li>Cap delay at <code>maxDelayMs</code> to avoid unbounded waits</li>\n<li>If all attempts fail, throw the last exception</li>\n<li>If an attempt succeeds, return the result immediately</li>\n</ul></div>\n<div class=\"req-box\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Delay Schedule (example)</div>\n<ul>\n<li>Attempt 1 fails → wait 100ms</li>\n<li>Attempt 2 fails → wait 200ms</li>\n<li>Attempt 3 fails → wait 400ms (or maxDelay, whichever is lower)</li>\n</ul></div>", "hints": ["Use a loop from 1 to maxAttempts. Wrap each attempt in try-catch.", "Track the current delay. After each failure (except the last), call delay(currentDelay) then multiply currentDelay by the multiplier. Use minOf(currentDelay, maxDelayMs) to cap it.", "The function signature should be generic: suspend fun <T> retryWithBackoff(..., block: suspend () -> T): T. Rethrow on last attempt by checking attempt == maxAttempts."], "approach": "<h3>Loop + Coroutine Delay</h3>\n<p>Loop through attempts. On success return early. On failure, if it's the last attempt rethrow. Otherwise compute delay = min(initialDelay × multiplier^(attempt-1), maxDelay), suspend with <code>delay()</code>, then continue.</p>\n<div class=\"miss-box\"><div class=\"miss-box-title\">What most candidates miss</div>\n<ul>\n<li>Retrying on ALL exceptions — in production you'd filter: retry only on transient errors, not 4xx client errors</li>\n<li>Not using <code>minOf</code> to cap the delay</li>\n<li>Jitter — adding a small random offset to delays prevents thundering herd in distributed systems</li>\n</ul></div>", "androidStudio": false, "editorCode": "import kotlinx.coroutines.*\n\n//sampleStart\nsuspend fun <T> retryWithBackoff(\n    maxAttempts: Int = 3,\n    initialDelayMs: Long = 100L,\n    multiplier: Double = 2.0,\n    maxDelayMs: Long = 5000L,\n    block: suspend () -> T\n): T {\n    // TODO: Retry block up to maxAttempts times with exponential backoff\n    // Delay grows: initialDelayMs, initialDelayMs*multiplier, initialDelayMs*multiplier^2...\n    // Cap delay at maxDelayMs\n    // Throw the last exception if all attempts fail\n    TODO(\"Implement retry logic\")\n}\n//sampleEnd\n\n// ---- Droidly test runner (hidden in the editor) ----\nprivate var passedCount = 0\nprivate var totalCount = 0\nprivate fun record(name: String, error: Throwable?) {\n    totalCount++\n    when (error) {\n        null -> { passedCount++; println(\"✓ $name\") }\n        is NotImplementedError -> println(\"✗ $name — not implemented yet\")\n        is AssertionError -> println(\"✗ $name — ${error.message}\")\n        else -> println(\"✗ $name — threw ${error::class.simpleName}: ${error.message}\")\n    }\n}\nfun test(name: String, body: () -> Unit) = record(name, runCatching(body).exceptionOrNull())\nfun <T> expect(actual: T, expected: T, what: String = \"\") {\n    if (actual != expected) throw AssertionError((if (what.isEmpty()) \"\" else \"$what: \") + \"expected $expected, got $actual\")\n}\nfun expectTrue(cond: Boolean, message: String) { if (!cond) throw AssertionError(message) }\nfun summary() {\n    println()\n    if (passedCount == totalCount) println(\"ALL \" + totalCount + \" TESTS PASSED\")\n    else println(\"\" + passedCount + \" of \" + totalCount + \" tests passed\")\n}\n\nsuspend fun testS(name: String, body: suspend () -> Unit) {\n    val err = try { body(); null } catch (e: Throwable) { e }\n    reportSuspend(name, err)\n}\nfun reportSuspend(name: String, err: Throwable?) = test(name) { if (err != null) throw err }\n\nfun main() = runBlocking {\n    testS(\"returns at once when the first attempt succeeds\") {\n        var calls = 0; val t = System.currentTimeMillis()\n        val r = retryWithBackoff(3, 100L) { calls++; \"ok\" }\n        expect(r, \"ok\"); expect(calls, 1, \"calls\"); expectTrue(System.currentTimeMillis() - t < 90, \"should not wait\")\n    }\n    testS(\"retries until it succeeds\") {\n        var calls = 0\n        val r = retryWithBackoff(3, 10L) { calls++; if (calls < 3) throw Exception(\"fail $calls\"); \"data\" }\n        expect(r, \"data\"); expect(calls, 3, \"calls\")\n    }\n    testS(\"throws the last exception after maxAttempts\") {\n        var calls = 0\n        val err = try { retryWithBackoff(3, 10L) { calls++; throw IllegalStateException(\"fail $calls\") }; null } catch (e: Exception) { e }\n        expect(err?.message, \"fail 3\", \"exception message\"); expect(calls, 3, \"calls\")\n    }\n    testS(\"waits initialDelay, then initialDelay × multiplier (about 150 ms total)\") {\n        val t = System.currentTimeMillis()\n        runCatching { retryWithBackoff(3, 50L, 2.0) { throw Exception(\"x\") } }\n        val ms = System.currentTimeMillis() - t\n        expectTrue(ms in 140..600, \"expected about 50 + 100 = 150 ms of waiting, got $ms ms\")\n    }\n    testS(\"caps each delay at maxDelayMs\") {\n        var calls = 0; val t = System.currentTimeMillis()\n        runCatching { retryWithBackoff(3, 100L, 10.0, maxDelayMs = 150L) { calls++; throw Exception(\"x\") } }\n        val ms = System.currentTimeMillis() - t\n        expect(calls, 3, \"attempts\")\n        expectTrue(ms in 230..700, \"expected about 100 + 150 = 250 ms, got $ms ms (is the delay capped?)\")\n    }\n    summary()\n}\n", "solution": "suspend fun <T> retryWithBackoff(\n    maxAttempts: Int = 3,\n    initialDelayMs: Long = 100L,\n    multiplier: Double = 2.0,\n    maxDelayMs: Long = 5000L,\n    block: suspend () -> T\n): T {\n    require(maxAttempts >= 1) { \"maxAttempts must be at least 1\" }\n    var nextDelay = initialDelayMs.toDouble()\n    repeat(maxAttempts - 1) {\n        try {\n            return block()\n        } catch (e: CancellationException) {\n            throw e                       // never swallow cancellation\n        } catch (e: Exception) {\n            delay(minOf(nextDelay.toLong(), maxDelayMs))\n            nextDelay *= multiplier\n        }\n    }\n    return block()                        // last attempt: let its exception propagate\n}\n", "tests": ["returns at once when the first attempt succeeds", "retries until it succeeds", "throws the last exception after maxAttempts", "waits initialDelay, then initialDelay × multiplier (about 150 ms total)", "caps each delay at maxDelayMs"]}, {"id": 6, "slug": "shopping-cart-with-discounts", "title": "Shopping Cart with Discounts", "difficulty": "Medium", "timeMin": 45, "summary": "Model a shopping cart with sealed-class discounts in Kotlin. Android machine coding interview question with hints, tests and a solution.", "description": "<h3>Problem</h3>\n<p>Design a <strong>Shopping Cart</strong> that supports multiple discount types using Kotlin's sealed classes.</p>\n<div class=\"req-box\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Discount Types</div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>PercentageOff</strong> — e.g. 20% off item price</li>\n<li><strong>FlatDiscount</strong> — e.g. ₹200 off the item</li>\n<li><strong>BuyXGetYFree</strong> — e.g. buy 2 get 1 free (pay for ceil(quantity / (buy+free) × buy) items)</li>\n</ul></div>\n<div class=\"req-box\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Functional Requirements</div>\n<ul>\n<li><code>addItem(item)</code> — Add to cart or increase quantity if already present</li>\n<li><code>removeItem(productId)</code> — Remove item from cart</li>\n<li><code>calculateTotal()</code> — Return total price after all discounts</li>\n<li><code>getAppliedDiscounts()</code> — Return map of productId → discount amount saved</li>\n</ul></div>", "hints": ["Use a sealed class for Discount types. Each subtype carries different parameters — this is exactly what sealed classes are designed for.", "In calculateTotal(), use a when expression on the Discount type for each item. For BuyXGetYFree: if you buy 3 with buy=2,free=1, you pay for 2.", "For BuyXGetYFree: paidQuantity = ceil(quantity / (buyQuantity + freeQuantity).toFloat()) * buyQuantity"], "approach": "<h3>Sealed Class Dispatch</h3>\n<p>Use <code>when (item.discount)</code> in calculateTotal. Each branch handles its discount math. Store items in a <code>MutableMap&lt;String, CartItem&gt;</code> for O(1) add/update/remove by productId.</p>\n<div class=\"miss-box\"><div class=\"miss-box-title\">What most candidates miss</div>\n<ul>\n<li>BuyXGetYFree calculation — most get the formula wrong for non-divisible quantities</li>\n<li>Flat discount exceeding item price — should floor at 0, not go negative</li>\n<li>Not handling duplicate addItem (should accumulate quantity, not replace)</li>\n</ul></div>", "androidStudio": false, "editorCode": "import kotlin.math.ceil\nimport kotlin.math.max\n\n//sampleStart\nsealed class Discount {\n    data class PercentageOff(val percentage: Double) : Discount()\n    data class FlatDiscount(val amount: Double) : Discount()\n    data class BuyXGetYFree(val buyQuantity: Int, val freeQuantity: Int) : Discount()\n    object None : Discount()\n}\n\ndata class CartItem(\n    val productId: String,\n    val name: String,\n    val price: Double,\n    val quantity: Int,\n    val discount: Discount = Discount.None\n)\n\nclass ShoppingCart {\n    // TODO: Implement the shopping cart\n\n    fun addItem(item: CartItem) {\n        TODO(\"Add item or update quantity if productId already exists\")\n    }\n\n    fun removeItem(productId: String) {\n        TODO(\"Remove item from cart\")\n    }\n\n    fun calculateTotal(): Double {\n        TODO(\"Return total price after applying all discounts\")\n    }\n\n    fun getAppliedDiscounts(): Map<String, Double> {\n        TODO(\"Return map of productId to discount amount saved\")\n    }\n}\n//sampleEnd\n\n// ---- Droidly test runner (hidden in the editor) ----\nprivate var passedCount = 0\nprivate var totalCount = 0\nprivate fun record(name: String, error: Throwable?) {\n    totalCount++\n    when (error) {\n        null -> { passedCount++; println(\"✓ $name\") }\n        is NotImplementedError -> println(\"✗ $name — not implemented yet\")\n        is AssertionError -> println(\"✗ $name — ${error.message}\")\n        else -> println(\"✗ $name — threw ${error::class.simpleName}: ${error.message}\")\n    }\n}\nfun test(name: String, body: () -> Unit) = record(name, runCatching(body).exceptionOrNull())\nfun <T> expect(actual: T, expected: T, what: String = \"\") {\n    if (actual != expected) throw AssertionError((if (what.isEmpty()) \"\" else \"$what: \") + \"expected $expected, got $actual\")\n}\nfun expectTrue(cond: Boolean, message: String) { if (!cond) throw AssertionError(message) }\nfun summary() {\n    println()\n    if (passedCount == totalCount) println(\"ALL \" + totalCount + \" TESTS PASSED\")\n    else println(\"\" + passedCount + \" of \" + totalCount + \" tests passed\")\n}\n\nfun near(a: Double, b: Double) = kotlin.math.abs(a - b) < 0.001\nfun main() {\n    test(\"an item without a discount costs price × quantity\") {\n        val c = ShoppingCart(); c.addItem(CartItem(\"pen\", \"Pen\", 10.0, 3)); expectTrue(near(c.calculateTotal(), 30.0), \"total ${c.calculateTotal()}, expected 30.0\")\n    }\n    test(\"PercentageOff: 2 × 1000 with 20% off = 1600\") {\n        val c = ShoppingCart(); c.addItem(CartItem(\"shirt\", \"Shirt\", 1000.0, 2, Discount.PercentageOff(20.0)))\n        expectTrue(near(c.calculateTotal(), 1600.0), \"total ${c.calculateTotal()}, expected 1600.0\")\n    }\n    test(\"FlatDiscount: 2000 − 200 = 1800\") {\n        val c = ShoppingCart(); c.addItem(CartItem(\"shoes\", \"Shoes\", 2000.0, 1, Discount.FlatDiscount(200.0)))\n        expectTrue(near(c.calculateTotal(), 1800.0), \"total ${c.calculateTotal()}, expected 1800.0\")\n    }\n    test(\"FlatDiscount larger than the price floors at 0\") {\n        val c = ShoppingCart(); c.addItem(CartItem(\"cap\", \"Cap\", 100.0, 1, Discount.FlatDiscount(300.0)))\n        expectTrue(near(c.calculateTotal(), 0.0), \"total ${c.calculateTotal()}, expected 0.0\")\n    }\n    test(\"BuyXGetYFree: buy 2 get 1 → 3 socks cost 2, 5 socks cost 4\") {\n        val c = ShoppingCart(); c.addItem(CartItem(\"socks\", \"Socks\", 100.0, 3, Discount.BuyXGetYFree(2, 1)))\n        expectTrue(near(c.calculateTotal(), 200.0), \"3 socks: total ${c.calculateTotal()}, expected 200.0\")\n        c.addItem(CartItem(\"socks\", \"Socks\", 100.0, 2, Discount.BuyXGetYFree(2, 1)))\n        expectTrue(near(c.calculateTotal(), 400.0), \"5 socks: total ${c.calculateTotal()}, expected 400.0\")\n    }\n    test(\"adding the same product again increases its quantity\") {\n        val c = ShoppingCart(); c.addItem(CartItem(\"pen\", \"Pen\", 10.0, 1)); c.addItem(CartItem(\"pen\", \"Pen\", 10.0, 2))\n        expectTrue(near(c.calculateTotal(), 30.0), \"total ${c.calculateTotal()}, expected 30.0\")\n    }\n    test(\"removeItem removes the product\") {\n        val c = ShoppingCart(); c.addItem(CartItem(\"pen\", \"Pen\", 10.0, 1)); c.addItem(CartItem(\"cap\", \"Cap\", 50.0, 1))\n        c.removeItem(\"pen\"); expectTrue(near(c.calculateTotal(), 50.0), \"total ${c.calculateTotal()}, expected 50.0\")\n    }\n    test(\"full cart total is 3600 and savings are listed per product\") {\n        val c = ShoppingCart()\n        c.addItem(CartItem(\"shirt\", \"Shirt\", 1000.0, 2, Discount.PercentageOff(20.0)))\n        c.addItem(CartItem(\"shoes\", \"Shoes\", 2000.0, 1, Discount.FlatDiscount(200.0)))\n        c.addItem(CartItem(\"socks\", \"Socks\", 100.0, 3, Discount.BuyXGetYFree(2, 1)))\n        expectTrue(near(c.calculateTotal(), 3600.0), \"total ${c.calculateTotal()}, expected 3600.0\")\n        val d = c.getAppliedDiscounts()\n        expectTrue(near(d[\"shirt\"] ?: -1.0, 400.0) && near(d[\"shoes\"] ?: -1.0, 200.0) && near(d[\"socks\"] ?: -1.0, 100.0), \"savings $d, expected shirt=400, shoes=200, socks=100\")\n    }\n    summary()\n}\n", "solution": "sealed class Discount {\n    data class PercentageOff(val percentage: Double) : Discount()\n    data class FlatDiscount(val amount: Double) : Discount()\n    data class BuyXGetYFree(val buyQuantity: Int, val freeQuantity: Int) : Discount()\n    object None : Discount()\n}\n\ndata class CartItem(\n    val productId: String,\n    val name: String,\n    val price: Double,\n    val quantity: Int,\n    val discount: Discount = Discount.None\n)\n\nclass ShoppingCart {\n    private val items = LinkedHashMap<String, CartItem>()\n\n    fun addItem(item: CartItem) {\n        val existing = items[item.productId]\n        items[item.productId] = existing?.copy(quantity = existing.quantity + item.quantity) ?: item\n    }\n\n    fun removeItem(productId: String) { items.remove(productId) }\n\n    fun calculateTotal(): Double = items.values.sumOf { lineTotal(it) - saving(it) }\n\n    fun getAppliedDiscounts(): Map<String, Double> =\n        items.values.associate { it.productId to saving(it) }.filterValues { it > 0.0 }\n\n    private fun lineTotal(item: CartItem) = item.price * item.quantity\n\n    private fun saving(item: CartItem): Double = when (val d = item.discount) {\n        is Discount.PercentageOff -> lineTotal(item) * d.percentage / 100.0\n        is Discount.FlatDiscount -> minOf(d.amount, lineTotal(item))          // never below zero\n        is Discount.BuyXGetYFree -> {\n            val group = d.buyQuantity + d.freeQuantity\n            val freeUnits = (item.quantity / group) * d.freeQuantity\n            freeUnits * item.price\n        }\n        Discount.None -> 0.0\n    }\n}\n", "tests": ["an item without a discount costs price × quantity", "PercentageOff: 2 × 1000 with 20% off = 1600", "FlatDiscount: 2000 − 200 = 1800", "FlatDiscount larger than the price floors at 0", "BuyXGetYFree: buy 2 get 1 → 3 socks cost 2, 5 socks cost 4", "adding the same product again increases its quantity", "removeItem removes the product", "full cart total is 3600 and savings are listed per product"]}, {"id": 7, "slug": "in-memory-cache-with-ttl", "title": "In-Memory Cache with TTL", "difficulty": "Medium", "timeMin": 35, "summary": "Build a generic in-memory cache with per-entry TTL in Kotlin. Android machine coding interview question with hints, tests and a solution.", "description": "<h3>Problem</h3>\n<p>Implement a <strong>generic in-memory cache with TTL (time-to-live)</strong> expiry for each entry.</p>\n<div class=\"req-box\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Functional Requirements</div>\n<ul>\n<li><code>put(key, value, ttlMs)</code> — Store entry with an expiry time (defaults to <code>defaultTtlMs</code>)</li>\n<li><code>get(key)</code> — Return value if key exists and not expired, otherwise <code>null</code></li>\n<li><code>evictExpired()</code> — Proactively remove all expired entries</li>\n<li><code>size()</code> — Return count of non-expired entries</li>\n</ul></div>\n<div class=\"req-box\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Expiry Rule</div>\n<p>An entry expires when <code>currentTime >= insertionTime + ttlMs</code>. Expired entries should not be returned by <code>get</code> even if not yet evicted.</p></div>", "hints": ["Store both the value and its expiry timestamp in a wrapper class.", "Use a data class: CacheEntry(value: V, expiryAt: Long). Compute expiryAt = System.currentTimeMillis() + ttlMs at insertion time.", "In get(), if entry exists but System.currentTimeMillis() >= entry.expiryAt, treat it as a miss (optionally remove it lazily). In size(), count only entries where expiryAt > currentTime."], "approach": "<h3>Lazy Expiry + Proactive Eviction</h3>\n<p>Store <code>Map&lt;K, CacheEntry&lt;V&gt;&gt;</code> where each entry carries its absolute expiry timestamp. Lazy expiry on <code>get</code> — check and return null if expired. <code>evictExpired()</code> does a full sweep.</p>\n<div class=\"miss-box\"><div class=\"miss-box-title\">What most candidates miss</div>\n<ul>\n<li>Thread safety — concurrent reads/writes need synchronization or ConcurrentHashMap</li>\n<li>size() returning stale count — must filter expired entries</li>\n<li>Not removing lazily-expired entries from the map (memory leak)</li>\n</ul></div>", "androidStudio": false, "editorCode": "//sampleStart\nclass TTLCache<K, V>(private val defaultTtlMs: Long = 5000L) {\n    // TODO: Implement cache with per-entry TTL\n    // Hint: Store a wrapper with the value AND its expiry timestamp\n\n    fun put(key: K, value: V, ttlMs: Long = defaultTtlMs) {\n        TODO(\"Store entry with expiry = currentTime + ttlMs\")\n    }\n\n    fun get(key: K): V? {\n        TODO(\"Return value if not expired, null otherwise\")\n    }\n\n    fun evictExpired() {\n        TODO(\"Remove all entries where currentTime >= expiryAt\")\n    }\n\n    fun size(): Int {\n        TODO(\"Return count of non-expired entries only\")\n    }\n}\n//sampleEnd\n\n// ---- Droidly test runner (hidden in the editor) ----\nprivate var passedCount = 0\nprivate var totalCount = 0\nprivate fun record(name: String, error: Throwable?) {\n    totalCount++\n    when (error) {\n        null -> { passedCount++; println(\"✓ $name\") }\n        is NotImplementedError -> println(\"✗ $name — not implemented yet\")\n        is AssertionError -> println(\"✗ $name — ${error.message}\")\n        else -> println(\"✗ $name — threw ${error::class.simpleName}: ${error.message}\")\n    }\n}\nfun test(name: String, body: () -> Unit) = record(name, runCatching(body).exceptionOrNull())\nfun <T> expect(actual: T, expected: T, what: String = \"\") {\n    if (actual != expected) throw AssertionError((if (what.isEmpty()) \"\" else \"$what: \") + \"expected $expected, got $actual\")\n}\nfun expectTrue(cond: Boolean, message: String) { if (!cond) throw AssertionError(message) }\nfun summary() {\n    println()\n    if (passedCount == totalCount) println(\"ALL \" + totalCount + \" TESTS PASSED\")\n    else println(\"\" + passedCount + \" of \" + totalCount + \" tests passed\")\n}\n\nfun main() {\n    test(\"get returns a fresh value\") { val c = TTLCache<String, String>(1000); c.put(\"a\", \"A\"); expect(c.get(\"a\"), \"A\") }\n    test(\"get returns null for a missing key\") { expect(TTLCache<String, String>().get(\"nope\"), null) }\n    test(\"an entry expires after its own TTL\") {\n        val c = TTLCache<String, String>(1000); c.put(\"a\", \"A\", ttlMs = 50); Thread.sleep(80); expect(c.get(\"a\"), null)\n    }\n    test(\"the default TTL is used when none is given\") {\n        val c = TTLCache<String, String>(defaultTtlMs = 50); c.put(\"a\", \"A\"); Thread.sleep(80); expect(c.get(\"a\"), null)\n    }\n    test(\"entries with a longer TTL stay alive\") {\n        val c = TTLCache<String, String>(1000); c.put(\"long\", \"L\"); c.put(\"short\", \"S\", 50); Thread.sleep(80)\n        expect(c.get(\"long\"), \"L\", \"long\"); expect(c.get(\"short\"), null, \"short\")\n    }\n    test(\"put on an existing key resets its value and TTL\") {\n        val c = TTLCache<String, String>(1000); c.put(\"a\", \"old\", 50); c.put(\"a\", \"new\", 1000); Thread.sleep(80); expect(c.get(\"a\"), \"new\")\n    }\n    test(\"size() counts only entries that have not expired\") {\n        val c = TTLCache<String, Int>(1000); c.put(\"a\", 1); c.put(\"b\", 2, 50); Thread.sleep(80); expect(c.size(), 1)\n    }\n    test(\"evictExpired() removes expired entries\") {\n        val c = TTLCache<String, Int>(1000); c.put(\"a\", 1, 50); c.put(\"b\", 2); Thread.sleep(80); c.evictExpired()\n        expect(c.size(), 1, \"size\"); expect(c.get(\"b\"), 2, \"b\")\n    }\n    summary()\n}\n", "solution": "class TTLCache<K, V>(private val defaultTtlMs: Long = 5000L) {\n    private data class Entry<V>(val value: V, val expiresAt: Long)\n\n    private val map = HashMap<K, Entry<V>>()\n\n    private fun now() = System.currentTimeMillis()\n\n    @Synchronized\n    fun put(key: K, value: V, ttlMs: Long = defaultTtlMs) {\n        map[key] = Entry(value, now() + ttlMs)\n    }\n\n    @Synchronized\n    fun get(key: K): V? {\n        val e = map[key] ?: return null\n        if (now() >= e.expiresAt) { map.remove(key); return null }   // lazy expiry\n        return e.value\n    }\n\n    @Synchronized\n    fun evictExpired() {\n        val t = now()\n        map.entries.removeIf { t >= it.value.expiresAt }\n    }\n\n    @Synchronized\n    fun size(): Int {\n        val t = now()\n        return map.values.count { t < it.expiresAt }\n    }\n}\n", "tests": ["get returns a fresh value", "get returns null for a missing key", "an entry expires after its own TTL", "the default TTL is used when none is given", "entries with a longer TTL stay alive", "put on an existing key resets its value and TTL", "size() counts only entries that have not expired", "evictExpired() removes expired entries"]}, {"id": 8, "slug": "order-state-machine", "title": "Order State Machine", "difficulty": "Medium", "timeMin": 35, "summary": "Implement a food-order state machine with Kotlin sealed classes. Android machine coding interview question with hints, tests and a solution.", "description": "<h3>Problem</h3>\n<p>Implement a <strong>finite state machine</strong> for a food delivery order lifecycle using Kotlin sealed classes.</p>\n<div class=\"req-box\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">State Transitions</div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Placed</strong> → (Confirm) → <strong>Confirmed</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Confirmed</strong> → (StartPreparing) → <strong>Preparing</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Preparing</strong> → (Dispatch) → <strong>OutForDelivery</strong></li>\n<li><strong>OutForDelivery</strong> → (MarkDelivered) → <strong>Delivered</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Any state except Delivered</strong> → (Cancel) → <strong>Cancelled</strong></li>\n</ul></div>\n<div class=\"req-box\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Functional Requirements</div>\n<ul>\n<li><code>transition(event)</code> — Apply event, return <code>true</code> if valid, <code>false</code> if invalid for current state</li>\n<li><code>getStatusDescription()</code> — Return a human-readable status string</li>\n<li>Invalid transitions must not change state</li>\n</ul></div>", "hints": ["Use sealed classes for both OrderState and OrderEvent. This gives exhaustive when expressions.", "In transition(), use a when(currentState) outer block, then when(event) inner block. Any unmatched combination returns false.", "The Cancel event is valid from most states — handle it in each non-terminal state's branch, or use an outer check before the main when block."], "approach": "<h3>Sealed Class State Machine</h3>\n<p>Use nested <code>when</code> expressions. Outer: current state. Inner: incoming event. Only valid pairs update <code>currentState</code> and return true. Everything else returns false without mutating state.</p>\n<div class=\"miss-box\"><div class=\"miss-box-title\">What most candidates miss</div>\n<ul>\n<li>Allowing Cancel from Delivered state — Delivered is terminal, nothing should transition out</li>\n<li>Not returning false for unrecognised events — a default else clause matters</li>\n<li>Missing the Cancelled → any transition (Cancelled is also terminal)</li>\n</ul></div>", "androidStudio": false, "editorCode": "//sampleStart\nsealed class OrderState {\n    object Placed : OrderState()\n    object Confirmed : OrderState()\n    object Preparing : OrderState()\n    object OutForDelivery : OrderState()\n    object Delivered : OrderState()\n    object Cancelled : OrderState()\n}\n\nsealed class OrderEvent {\n    object Confirm : OrderEvent()\n    object StartPreparing : OrderEvent()\n    object Dispatch : OrderEvent()\n    object MarkDelivered : OrderEvent()\n    object Cancel : OrderEvent()\n}\n\nclass OrderStateMachine(initialState: OrderState = OrderState.Placed) {\n    var currentState: OrderState = initialState\n        private set\n\n    // TODO: Implement state transitions\n    // Return true if transition was valid, false if invalid for current state\n    // Invalid transitions must NOT change currentState\n    fun transition(event: OrderEvent): Boolean {\n        TODO(\"Implement using sealed class when expressions\")\n    }\n\n    fun getStatusDescription(): String = when (currentState) {\n        is OrderState.Placed         -> \"Order placed, awaiting confirmation\"\n        is OrderState.Confirmed      -> \"Order confirmed by restaurant\"\n        is OrderState.Preparing      -> \"Your food is being prepared 👨‍🍳\"\n        is OrderState.OutForDelivery -> \"Out for delivery 🛵\"\n        is OrderState.Delivered      -> \"Delivered! Enjoy your meal 🍱\"\n        is OrderState.Cancelled      -> \"Order cancelled\"\n    }\n}\n//sampleEnd\n\n// ---- Droidly test runner (hidden in the editor) ----\nprivate var passedCount = 0\nprivate var totalCount = 0\nprivate fun record(name: String, error: Throwable?) {\n    totalCount++\n    when (error) {\n        null -> { passedCount++; println(\"✓ $name\") }\n        is NotImplementedError -> println(\"✗ $name — not implemented yet\")\n        is AssertionError -> println(\"✗ $name — ${error.message}\")\n        else -> println(\"✗ $name — threw ${error::class.simpleName}: ${error.message}\")\n    }\n}\nfun test(name: String, body: () -> Unit) = record(name, runCatching(body).exceptionOrNull())\nfun <T> expect(actual: T, expected: T, what: String = \"\") {\n    if (actual != expected) throw AssertionError((if (what.isEmpty()) \"\" else \"$what: \") + \"expected $expected, got $actual\")\n}\nfun expectTrue(cond: Boolean, message: String) { if (!cond) throw AssertionError(message) }\nfun summary() {\n    println()\n    if (passedCount == totalCount) println(\"ALL \" + totalCount + \" TESTS PASSED\")\n    else println(\"\" + passedCount + \" of \" + totalCount + \" tests passed\")\n}\n\nfun main() {\n    test(\"the happy path: Placed → Confirmed → Preparing → OutForDelivery → Delivered\") {\n        val o = OrderStateMachine()\n        expect(o.transition(OrderEvent.Confirm), true, \"Confirm\"); expect(o.transition(OrderEvent.StartPreparing), true, \"StartPreparing\")\n        expect(o.transition(OrderEvent.Dispatch), true, \"Dispatch\"); expect(o.transition(OrderEvent.MarkDelivered), true, \"MarkDelivered\")\n        expect(o.currentState, OrderState.Delivered as OrderState, \"final state\")\n    }\n    test(\"an invalid event returns false and keeps the state\") {\n        val o = OrderStateMachine(); expect(o.transition(OrderEvent.MarkDelivered), false); expect(o.currentState, OrderState.Placed as OrderState)\n    }\n    test(\"steps cannot be skipped\") {\n        val o = OrderStateMachine(); o.transition(OrderEvent.Confirm)\n        expect(o.transition(OrderEvent.Dispatch), false, \"Dispatch from Confirmed\"); expect(o.currentState, OrderState.Confirmed as OrderState)\n    }\n    test(\"Cancel works from every active state\") {\n        val paths = listOf(listOf<OrderEvent>(), listOf(OrderEvent.Confirm), listOf(OrderEvent.Confirm, OrderEvent.StartPreparing),\n            listOf(OrderEvent.Confirm, OrderEvent.StartPreparing, OrderEvent.Dispatch))\n        for (p in paths) { val o = OrderStateMachine(); p.forEach { o.transition(it) }\n            expect(o.transition(OrderEvent.Cancel), true, \"Cancel after ${p.size} steps\"); expect(o.currentState, OrderState.Cancelled as OrderState) }\n    }\n    test(\"Delivered is final: nothing moves it, not even Cancel\") {\n        val o = OrderStateMachine(OrderState.Delivered)\n        listOf(OrderEvent.Cancel, OrderEvent.Confirm, OrderEvent.Dispatch).forEach { expect(o.transition(it), false, \"event ${it::class.simpleName}\") }\n        expect(o.currentState, OrderState.Delivered as OrderState)\n    }\n    test(\"Cancelled is final\") {\n        val o = OrderStateMachine(OrderState.Cancelled); expect(o.transition(OrderEvent.Confirm), false); expect(o.transition(OrderEvent.Cancel), false)\n    }\n    test(\"status text follows the state\") {\n        val o = OrderStateMachine(); o.transition(OrderEvent.Confirm); expect(o.getStatusDescription(), \"Order confirmed by restaurant\")\n    }\n    summary()\n}\n", "solution": "sealed class OrderState {\n    object Placed : OrderState()\n    object Confirmed : OrderState()\n    object Preparing : OrderState()\n    object OutForDelivery : OrderState()\n    object Delivered : OrderState()\n    object Cancelled : OrderState()\n}\n\nsealed class OrderEvent {\n    object Confirm : OrderEvent()\n    object StartPreparing : OrderEvent()\n    object Dispatch : OrderEvent()\n    object MarkDelivered : OrderEvent()\n    object Cancel : OrderEvent()\n}\n\nclass OrderStateMachine(initialState: OrderState = OrderState.Placed) {\n    var currentState: OrderState = initialState\n        private set\n\n    fun transition(event: OrderEvent): Boolean {\n        val next: OrderState? = when (val s = currentState) {\n            OrderState.Delivered, OrderState.Cancelled -> null                // terminal states\n            else -> when (event) {\n                OrderEvent.Cancel -> OrderState.Cancelled\n                OrderEvent.Confirm -> if (s == OrderState.Placed) OrderState.Confirmed else null\n                OrderEvent.StartPreparing -> if (s == OrderState.Confirmed) OrderState.Preparing else null\n                OrderEvent.Dispatch -> if (s == OrderState.Preparing) OrderState.OutForDelivery else null\n                OrderEvent.MarkDelivered -> if (s == OrderState.OutForDelivery) OrderState.Delivered else null\n            }\n        }\n        if (next == null) return false\n        currentState = next\n        return true\n    }\n\n    fun getStatusDescription(): String = when (currentState) {\n        is OrderState.Placed         -> \"Order placed, awaiting confirmation\"\n        is OrderState.Confirmed      -> \"Order confirmed by restaurant\"\n        is OrderState.Preparing      -> \"Your food is being prepared 👨‍🍳\"\n        is OrderState.OutForDelivery -> \"Out for delivery 🛵\"\n        is OrderState.Delivered      -> \"Delivered! Enjoy your meal 🍱\"\n        is OrderState.Cancelled      -> \"Order cancelled\"\n    }\n}\n", "tests": ["the happy path: Placed → Confirmed → Preparing → OutForDelivery → Delivered", "an invalid event returns false and keeps the state", "steps cannot be skipped", "Cancel works from every active state", "Delivered is final: nothing moves it, not even Cancel", "Cancelled is final", "status text follows the state"]}, {"id": 9, "slug": "restaurant-bill-screen", "title": "Restaurant Bill Screen", "difficulty": "Hard", "timeMin": 60, "summary": "Build a restaurant bill screen on Android: Repository, StateFlow, ViewModel and RecyclerView. A UI machine coding interview challenge with hints.", "description": "<h3>Problem</h3>\n<p>Design and implement the restaurant bill screen below. Fetch bill data from a dummy API (simulated with a <strong>1.5s delay</strong>), show a loading state, then render the check. This is a UI-focused machine coding challenge.</p>\n\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:20px;align-items:flex-start;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:14px 0\">\n  <div style=\"flex-shrink:0\">\n    <div style=\"font-size:10px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:6px;text-align:center\">Target Screen</div>\n    <div style=\"width:180px;border:2px solid #d0d0d0;border-radius:18px;overflow:hidden;background:#f5f5f5;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.12)\">\n      <div style=\"background:#e0e0e0;height:8px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center\">\n        <div style=\"width:40px;height:4px;border-radius:2px;background:#bbb\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"background:#FFFFFF;padding:10px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid #eeeeee\">\n        <span style=\"color:#404040;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif\">Toast</span>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"background:#fff;padding:0 12px;min-height:120px\">\n        <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:7px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #f2f2f2;font-size:11px;color:#404040;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif\"><span>Burger</span><span>$8.99</span></div>\n        <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:7px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #f2f2f2;font-size:11px;color:#404040;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif\"><span>Fries</span><span>$3.49</span></div>\n        <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:7px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #f2f2f2;font-size:11px;color:#404040;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif\"><span>Soda</span><span>$1.99</span></div>\n        <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:7px 0;font-size:11px;color:#404040;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif\"><span>Ice Cream</span><span>$1.99</span></div>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"background:#FFFFFF;padding:10px 12px;border-top:1px solid #eeeeee\">\n        <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:8px;font-size:11px;color:#404040;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif\"><span>Total:</span><span>$15.67</span></div>\n        <div style=\"display:flex;gap:6px\">\n          <div style=\"flex:1;height:32px;background:#022CFA;border-radius:4px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:#fff;font-size:11px;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif\">Print</div>\n          <div style=\"flex:1;height:32px;background:#022CFA;border-radius:4px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:#fff;font-size:11px;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif\">Pay $15.67</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"background:#e0e0e0;height:8px\"></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"flex:1;min-width:0\">\n    <div class=\"req-box\" style=\"margin-bottom:8px\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Header</div>\n    <ul style=\"margin:0\">\n      <li>Background: <code>#FFFFFF</code> · Padding: <code>12dp</code></li>\n      <li>\"Toast\" text — color <code>#404040</code>, size <code>16sp</code></li>\n    </ul></div>\n    <div class=\"req-box\" style=\"margin-bottom:8px\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Item List (RecyclerView)</div>\n    <ul style=\"margin:0\">\n      <li>Each row: item name (left) + price (right)</li>\n      <li>Scrollable — list length is dynamic from API</li>\n      <li>Show <strong>loading spinner</strong> while fetching</li>\n    </ul></div>\n    <div class=\"req-box\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Footer</div>\n    <ul style=\"margin:0\">\n      <li>Background: <code>#FFFFFF</code> · Padding: <code>12dp</code></li>\n      <li>Total text — color <code>#404040</code>, size <code>16sp</code></li>\n      <li>Two buttons side by side · Height: <code>48dp</code></li>\n      <li>Margin top (from total): <code>8dp</code> · Between buttons: <code>8dp</code></li>\n      <li>Button bg: <code>#022CFA</code> · Text: <code>#FFFFFF</code>, size <code>16sp</code></li>\n    </ul></div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"req-box\"><div class=\"req-box-title\">Dummy API — Mock this in your Repository</div>\n<pre style=\"font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:11.5px;margin:0;line-height:1.7;overflow-x:auto\">{\n  \"items\": [\n    { \"name\": \"Burger\",    \"price\": 8.99 },\n    { \"name\": \"Fries\",     \"price\": 3.49 },\n    { \"name\": \"Soda\",      \"price\": 1.99 },\n    { \"name\": \"Ice Cream\", \"price\": 1.99 }\n  ],\n  \"total\": 15.67\n}\n<span style=\"color:var(--muted)\">// Simulate network latency: delay(1500) before emitting data</span></pre></div>\n\n<h3>Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Architecture: <strong>MVVM</strong> — ViewModel + Repository + sealed UiState</li>\n<li>Use <code>StateFlow</code> in ViewModel, collect with <code>repeatOnLifecycle(STARTED)</code></li>\n<li>Use <code>StateFlow.update { }</code> — not <code>.value =</code></li>\n<li>Repository returns <code>Flow&lt;CheckData&gt;</code> with <code>delay(1500)</code></li>\n<li>Handle Loading → Success → Error states in the UI</li>\n<li>Total amount and Pay button text must come from API data — do not hardcode</li>\n</ul>", "hints": ["Start with data models: <code>data class CheckItem(val name: String, val price: Double)</code> and <code>CheckData(items, total)</code>. Then define a sealed <code>CheckUiState</code> with Loading, Success(data), Error(message).", "Repository: <code>fun getCheck(): Flow&lt;CheckData&gt; = flow { delay(1500); emit(mockData) }</code>. ViewModel: <code>private val _state = MutableStateFlow&lt;CheckUiState&gt;(Loading)</code> — call <code>.update{}</code> never <code>.value =</code>.", "In the Activity: <code>lifecycleScope.launch { repeatOnLifecycle(STARTED) { vm.state.collect { when(it) { ... } } } }</code>. On Loading → show ProgressBar, hide RecyclerView. On Success → reverse + call <code>adapter.submitList()</code> + update footer text.", "Footer layout: parent <code>LinearLayout</code> with <code>weightSum=\"2\"</code>, each button <code>layout_weight=\"1\"</code>. Pay button text = <code>\"Pay $\" + String.format(\"%.2f\", total)</code> — read from state, not hardcoded."], "approach": "<h3>Architecture Flow</h3>\n<p>Repository <code>flow { delay(1500); emit(data) }</code> → ViewModel collects + maps to <code>CheckUiState</code> via <code>MutableStateFlow.update{}</code> → Activity collects with <code>repeatOnLifecycle(STARTED)</code> → UI renders per state.</p>\n<h3>Key Files</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>CheckItem.kt / CheckData.kt</strong> — data models</li>\n<li><strong>CheckUiState.kt</strong> — sealed class with Loading, Success, Error</li>\n<li><strong>CheckRepository.kt</strong> — interface + impl with <code>Flow</code> + <code>delay(1500)</code></li>\n<li><strong>CheckViewModel.kt</strong> — MutableStateFlow + viewModelScope + .update{}</li>\n<li><strong>BillActivity.kt</strong> — repeatOnLifecycle + adapter + footer update</li>\n<li><strong>activity_bill.xml</strong> — header / FrameLayout(RecyclerView + ProgressBar) / footer</li>\n<li><strong>item_check_row.xml</strong> — two TextViews, horizontal LinearLayout</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"miss-box\"><div class=\"miss-box-title\">What most candidates miss</div>\n<ul>\n<li>Using <code>.value =</code> instead of <code>.update { }</code> — not atomic</li>\n<li>Collecting Flow in <code>onCreate</code> scope — leaks coroutine when app is backgrounded</li>\n<li>Hardcoding <code>\"Pay $15.67\"</code> — interviewer WILL change the mock data to test this</li>\n<li>Not handling Error state — ProgressBar keeps spinning if the API call fails</li>\n<li>ProgressBar outside FrameLayout — it won't overlay the RecyclerView properly</li>\n</ul></div>", "androidStudio": true, "editorCode": "// Write your Android implementation here.\n//\n// Suggested order:\n//   1. Data models (CheckItem, CheckData)\n//   2. Sealed UiState class\n//   3. Repository (Flow + delay)\n//   4. ViewModel (StateFlow + update)\n//   5. Activity + RecyclerView adapter\n//   6. XML layouts (activity_bill.xml, item_check_row.xml)\n\nfun main() {\n    println(\"Open in Android Studio to run the full UI implementation.\")\n}", "solution": null, "tests": []}];
